<h1 class="ct-art-title">Bringing Africa and the world to Ostrava: the AfrOstrava case study</h1>
<p class="ct-art-dek">A brand, a website and a year-round social engine for a new multicultural festival, seen by 171.1K people before the gates opened.</p>
<div class="ct-art-meta"><img alt="" src="/img/team-subomi.webp"/><span>Olasubomi Archibong</span><span class="dot"></span><span>5 min read</span></div>
</div>
<img alt="AfrOstrava Festival: brand, website and social campaign" class="ct-art-cover" src="/img/work-afrostrava-cover.webp"/>
</div>
</section>
<section class="section ct-art-body">
<div class="container w-layout-blockcontainer">
<div class="ct-art-col">
<div class="ct-art-stats">
<div><b>171.1K</b><span>Viewers reached</span></div>
<div><b>368.5K</b><span>Views in the run-up to the festival</span></div>
<div><b>184</b><span>Instagram posts</span></div>
<div><b>1,722</b><span>Instagram followers, built from scratch</span></div>
</div>
<p class="ct-art-lead">AfrOstrava is a multicultural festival that brings African music, dance, fashion, art and food to Ostrava, in the former ironworks of Lower Vítkovice. It needed a brand, a home online and a voice that would carry it all year, not just on the weekend of 14 to 15 August 2026. We built all three.</p>
<h2>The challenge</h2>
<p>A new festival had to win over a new city. AfrOstrava had to introduce African culture to a Czech audience, earn the trust of partners and sell tickets months before the gates opened. Three things had to be true at once.</p>
<ol class="ct-art-list">
<li><b>Credible from day one.</b> A brand that partners, sponsors and the city could put their name to.</li>
<li><b>Two audiences, one voice.</b> Czech locals and the African and expat community, in Czech and English.</li>
<li><b>Loud all year.</b> Momentum for months before the festival, and between editions.</li>
</ol>
<h2>The idea: a brand as loud as the festival</h2>
<p>Music, dance, fashion, art and gastronomy under one roof needed a brand with energy. A warped, hand-lettered wordmark moves like the music. A red, black and cream palette, organic blob shapes and torn-paper edges run across the site and socials. Sunburst frames and bold type give every artist and announcement the feel of the festival itself.</p>
<blockquote class="ct-art-quote">A multicultural celebration that brings Africa and the world to Ostrava.</blockquote>
<h2>The system</h2>
<h3>1. One home for tickets, partners and volunteers</h3>
<p>afrostrava.cz carries the brand into a site that does the selling. Every section ends in a ticket or partner button, with dedicated paths for volunteers, partners, past events, FAQs and a newsletter. The venue story, a former ironworks that is now a cultural landmark, gives the festival a sense of place.</p>
<div class="ct-art-figs one"><figure class="ct-art-fig"><img alt="afrostrava.cz hero: aerial view of the festival stage and crowd" loading="lazy" src="/img/af-web-hero.webp"/><figcaption>The homepage: a multicultural celebration that brings Africa and the world to Ostrava.</figcaption></figure></div>
<div class="ct-art-figs one"><figure class="ct-art-fig"><img alt="Three photo cards: a live music stage, an art installation and a dance class" loading="lazy" src="/img/af-web-experiences.webp"/><figcaption>Experiences that connect cultures: music, art, dance.</figcaption></figure></div>
<div class="ct-art-figs one"><figure class="ct-art-fig"><img alt="The Dolní Vítkovice ironworks at dusk beside the venue text" loading="lazy" src="/img/af-web-venue.webp"/><figcaption>The venue story: a former ironworks, now a cultural landmark.</figcaption></figure></div>
<h3>2. Every artist, a moment</h3>
<p>One template system covered every beat of the festival campaign: the headliner reveal, led by the CKay announcement, a card for each artist, countdowns from 47 days out and ticket offers to drive early sales.</p>
<div class="ct-art-figs three"><figure class="ct-art-fig"><img alt="Headliner CKay announcement post" loading="lazy" src="/img/af-headliner.webp"/><figcaption>Headliner reveal.</figcaption></figure><figure class="ct-art-fig"><img alt="Poster: CKay bude headlinerem festivalu AfrOstrava 2026" loading="lazy" src="/img/af-ckay-poster.webp"/><figcaption>Headliner poster.</figcaption></figure><figure class="ct-art-fig"><img alt="Artist card for Iska Muse on an orange sunburst" loading="lazy" src="/img/af-artist-iska.webp"/><figcaption>Artist cards.</figcaption></figure></div>
<div class="ct-art-figs three"><figure class="ct-art-fig"><img alt="Countdown post: 47 days left" loading="lazy" src="/img/af-countdown-47.webp"/><figcaption>Countdowns.</figcaption></figure><figure class="ct-art-fig"><img alt="Ticket offer post: 40 percent off" loading="lazy" src="/img/af-offer.webp"/><figcaption>Ticket offers.</figcaption></figure><figure class="ct-art-fig"><img alt="Weekend teaser: Taste Africa in one weekend" loading="lazy" src="/img/af-weekend.webp"/><figcaption>Weekend teaser.</figcaption></figure></div>
<h3>3. Always on, between festivals</h3>
<p>Instead of going quiet after the festival, the account ran a programme: Afro dance workshops, Connecting Cultures panels in Ostrava, curated playlists and stories about African heritage. That is how it reached 184 posts and kept the community growing all year.</p>
<div class="ct-art-figs three"><figure class="ct-art-fig"><img alt="Afro Dance Workshop announcement" loading="lazy" src="/img/af-dance.webp"/><figcaption>Afro dance workshops.</figcaption></figure><figure class="ct-art-fig"><img alt="Connecting Cultures in Ostrava panel discussion card" loading="lazy" src="/img/af-panel.webp"/><figcaption>Connecting Cultures panels.</figcaption></figure><figure class="ct-art-fig"><img alt="AfrOstrava community playlist post" loading="lazy" src="/img/af-playlist.webp"/><figcaption>Community playlists.</figcaption></figure></div>
<div class="ct-art-figs three"><figure class="ct-art-fig"><img alt="Culture post: Before the cloud, there were griots" loading="lazy" src="/img/af-griots.webp"/><figcaption>Culture stories.</figcaption></figure><figure class="ct-art-fig"><img alt="Culture post: Afro-Peruvian instruments" loading="lazy" src="/img/af-instruments.webp"/><figcaption>Heritage carousels.</figcaption></figure><figure class="ct-art-fig"><img alt="Creator spotlight post" loading="lazy" src="/img/af-spotlight.webp"/><figcaption>Creator spotlights.</figcaption></figure></div>
<h2>The results</h2>
<p>In the run-up to the festival, the content was seen by 171.1K people and viewed 368.5K times. Instagram drove the community and Facebook drove the clicks: together that is 10.9K link clicks and 15.3K profile visits, and 1,722 Instagram followers built from scratch.</p>
<div class="ct-art-results">
<div><span>Profile visits</span><b>12.4K Instagram, 2.9K Facebook</b><i style="--w:100%"></i></div>
<div><span>Content interactions</span><b>10.9K Instagram, 1.3K Facebook</b><i style="--w:88%"></i></div>
<div><span>Link clicks</span><b>4.5K Instagram, 6.4K Facebook</b><i style="--w:52%"></i></div>
<div><span>New follows</span><b>1.2K Instagram, 142 Facebook</b><i style="--w:12%"></i></div>
</div>
<h2>What we took from it</h2>
<ul class="ct-art-list">
<li><b>Make the brand as loud as the room.</b> A festival identity has to carry the energy of the weekend into every post.</li>
<li><b>Design every page to sell.</b> When each section ends in a ticket or partner button, the site works as hard as the campaign.</li>
<li><b>Don't go quiet between editions.</b> A year-round programme is what turns an audience into a community.</li>
</ul>
